cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "FastICGN"
abstract: >-
  FastICGN is a GPU-accelerated, sequence-oriented digital image correlation
  (DIC) implementation for long image sequences, built on OpenCorr. It
  reproduces the OpenCorr CPU reference measurement definition (FFTCC seeding
  plus IC-GN refinement with a first-order shape function) while keeping
  reference-image state, gradients and Hessians resident on the GPU across
  frames, and adds raw binary output, integrity manifests and an agent-operable
  command-line and MCP interface. The executables keep their historical
  opencorr_cli_* names.
type: software
